Since no release schedule was provided, here's a standard release milestone track (relative to launch day) you can map your real dates onto:

:::intelligent-ui{v="1"}
root = Stack([tl1, p1])
tl1 = Timeline("Release milestones", [m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8])
m1 = {title:"Scope locked", timestamp:"T-21d", description:"Feature list frozen, out-of-scope items moved to next train", status:"done"}
m2 = {title:"Code freeze", timestamp:"T-14d", description:"No new features; bug fixes and hardening only", status:"done"}
m3 = {title:"Feature complete / Beta", timestamp:"T-10d", description:"Beta cut, internal dogfooding and early access", status:"done"}
m4 = {title:"Release candidate", timestamp:"T-7d", description:"RC1 built, full regression suite run", status:"active"}
m5 = {title:"QA sign-off", timestamp:"T-4d", description:"No open blockers; all Sev-1/Sev-2 resolved", status:"pending"}
m6 = {title:"Staging verification", timestamp:"T-2d", description:"Smoke tests, migration rehearsal, rollback drill", status:"pending"}
m7 = {title:"Production rollout", timestamp:"T-0", description:"Staged rollout 10% → 50% → 100% with monitoring gates", status:"pending"}
m8 = {title:"Post-release review", timestamp:"T+5d", description:"Metrics vs. goals, retro, incident follow-ups", status:"pending"}
p1 = Progress("Release readiness", 42, "3 of 8 milestones complete")
:::

The gating milestones are **QA sign-off** and **staging verification** — those are the two that decide whether the rollout date holds. If a milestone slips, the usual lever is cutting scope at T-21d rather than pushing T-0.

