Here's a side-by-side view of the three hyperscalers, then a decision table on the dimensions that usually matter.

:::intelligent-ui{v="1"}
root = Stack([c1, t1])
c1 = Comparison("Cloud platforms at a glance", [aws, gcp, azure])
aws = {name: "AWS", attributes: ["Broadest, most mature service catalog", "Largest partner & talent ecosystem", "Strong enterprise, gov and compliance coverage", "Most complex pricing and IAM model"]}
gcp = {name: "Google Cloud", attributes: ["Best-in-class data, analytics and AI/ML", "GKE — the reference Kubernetes platform", "Excellent global network and price-performance", "Smallest enterprise footprint of the three"]}
azure = {name: "Microsoft Azure", attributes: ["Deepest Microsoft, Windows and Entra ID integration", "Leading hybrid story via Arc and Azure Stack", "Often cheapest for existing Microsoft licensing", "Widest global region coverage"]}
t1 = Table("Where each one wins", ["Dimension", "AWS", "Google Cloud", "Azure"], [["Core strength", "Breadth & maturity", "Data, AI/ML, Kubernetes", "Microsoft & hybrid"], ["Serverless", "Lambda (most mature)", "Cloud Run / Functions", "Azure Functions"], ["Managed Kubernetes", "EKS", "GKE (best-in-class)", "AKS"], ["Analytics", "Broad but more assembly required", "BigQuery", "Synapse / Fabric"], ["AI platform", "Bedrock + SageMaker", "Vertex AI + TPU", "Azure OpenAI / AI Foundry"], ["Discount model", "Savings Plans, RIs", "Sustained-use, CUDs", "Reservations + Azure Hybrid Benefit"], ["Region footprint", "Widest after Azure", "Fewer than AWS/Azure", "Widest"], ["Best fit", "Generalist at scale", "Data/AI-first teams", "Microsoft-centric enterprises"]])
:::

Short version: pick **AWS** when you need the widest service coverage and hiring pool, **GCP** when analytics, ML or Kubernetes is the centre of gravity, and **Azure** when you're already a Microsoft shop or need hybrid/on-prem integration. Multi-cloud is common in practice — landing on one primary and one secondary is usually a better trade-off than spreading evenly across all three.
